  "details": "<p>Lake Regillus is included as a toponym on Map 43 of the <em>Barrington Atlas.\u00a0</em>In the\u00a0<em>Barrington Atlas Directory,\u00a0</em>the compilers assert one theory for the location of the ancient lake, which is that it corresponds with the area now known as \"Pantano Secco\". The compilers further note that this assertion is an \"approximate location; no lake marked\".\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient lake in Latium that was the site of a Roman military victory in 496 BC; the precise location of the lake cannot be determined, although some scholars place its location at Pantano Secco near Frascati, Italy.",
  "reprPoint": [
